# L §5.10 point 1, E §4.2 step 5 (tally 2.1.2, issue #46): a reading at the start is in the day's first batch, taken
# together. y is stated at -5.00 PLN at 2026-01-15 start, padded from world, and nothing else moves it that day: after
# the batch it breaks its rule, so its pad is refused (`<place> is <b> after the day's observations and plans of <d>`)
# (q). z is stated at -5.00 PLN at the same instant and top puts 10.00 PLN in that day: the batch leaves 5.00 PLN, which
# stands (r), as a plan that arises and is paid on one day nets inside it. tally 2.1.1's refcore: q (20.00, -5.00) PLN.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
source bk "bank"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place y: claims PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place z: claims PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 2026-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input day: date
input day2: date

move top: transfers
  on day2
  leg cash from world to z amount amt

move p: transfers
  on day
  reads y, z
  leg cash from world to y amount amt + 0 * bal(y) + 0 * bal(z)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 10.00 PLN
  day = 2026-02-10
  day2 = 2026-01-15
  opening[y] = 20.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[z] = 20.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start

version st
  cite bk
  governs 2026-01
  known 2026-03-02
  pad y from world
  pad z from world
  stated[y] = -5.00 PLN at 2026-01-15 start
  stated[z] = -5.00 PLN at 2026-01-15 start
ask q: bal(y, 2026-01-14), bal(y, 2026-01-15)
ask r: bal(z, 2026-01-15)
=== expect
q: (20.00 PLN, refused: RUN-PLACE y is -5.00 PLN after the day's observations and plans of 2026-01-15)
  pad: y 2026-01-15 start, pads:st:y@2026-01-15 start of -25.00 PLN
  cut 2026-06-30
r: 5.00 PLN
  pad: z 2026-01-15 start, pads:st:z@2026-01-15 start of -25.00 PLN
  unfulfilled: top
  cut 2026-06-30
